<title>NEW ZEALAND: Grocorp amendment widens full year loss.</title>
<headline>Grocorp amendment widens full year loss.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amended year result to Sept 30</p>
<p>			   (million NZ$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss			  1.30 vs 2.05 loss</p>
<p>Note - Grocorp earlier reported a net loss of NZ$625,000 for the period, based on its best estimate of likely final net returns to growers from the New Zealand Apple and Pear Marketing Board. It said the widening of the loss was due to an unexpectedly reduced final payout from the Board.</p>
<p>The final result was made up of an operating profit of $0.74 million, offset by restructuring costs of $2.04 million relating to non-apple trading activities.</p>
</text>
